      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given your concerns about the air feeling \"thick,\" it is worth investigating if the misting system is aerosolizing anything beyond plain water or beneficial nutrients. While hydroponics is for plants, these powerful aerosolizing systems *could* technically be used to disperse fine particles, whether agricultural or otherwise. If you suspect anything other than plant mist is being dispersed, documenting the timing and characteristics of the release and speaking with local authorities might be a wise step.",
